WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.860
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.990
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.790
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.290
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.140
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.280
That's the Yamato!

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:41.240
We might as well make a grand entrance...

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.490
...and land right in the middle of fleet headquarters.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.750
Land on Yamato? But which part?

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.080
In terms of space and strength, the rear deck should do.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.510
That's interesting. Let's have a go at it then!

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.850
Guadalcanal Island

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.810
The Admiral's flag is on Yamato.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.400
That means that the Commander's on board.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.360
Roger that.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.610
Oh no!

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.370
Those fellas are heading for the harbor!

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.750
Port side 4 o'clock! Unidentified aircraft!

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.290
Ready the anti-air systems!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.170
Start up engines!

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.130
This is not a drill!

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.800
I'm going to put some distance between us.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.430
We're going to have some flight turbulence.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.100
Port side, aircraft passing by!

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.860
That was impressive, Lieutenant Satake.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.400
Thank you.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.860
I'm gonna make another round and prepare for landing.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.990
Yes. Please.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.380
Are they from the Allied forces?!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.340
We have an incoming from Natsushima Island.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.310
Wait a minute! Lieutenant Kusaka is on that auto-gyro!

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.930
Imperial Navy
Natsushima Headquarters

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:23.970
Imperial Navy
Natsushima Headquarters

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.730
I just had visual confirmation myself!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.020
Contact all vessels!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.770
The aircraft in sight is friendly.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.780
Inform the defense unit.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.860
Firing at the aircraft is prohibited! You got that?!

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.660
Petty Chief Officer Kawamoto!

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.870
Why's the Lieutenant risking a landing on the Yamato?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.500
We're about to begin writing...

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.420
...a brand new history!

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.800
This is the world's largest battleship.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.510
Watch out for the wires.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.720
Roger.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.970
Changing tilt by 90 degrees. Beginning descent!

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.270
What?! The wings are bent?!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.020
It stopped in mid-air?!

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.980
Gear down!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.200
All green!

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.540
Well done there, Lieutenant Satake.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.790
But there's no one around.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.840
What do we do now, Lieutenant?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.210
Don't worry, someone will come.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.220
Who will come?

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.180
The person with the greatest sense of curiosity on this ship.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.400
Imperial Navy Lieutenant Takumi Kusaka reporting!

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.570
It's been quite a long wait.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.440
Thank you for the personal welcome.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.990
So this is the auto-gyro 60 years later?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.920
What a huge propeller.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.080
What's this armament?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.500
Yes. It's a 20mm Triple-barrel Vulcan.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.720
It must take years of training to fly a plane like this.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.680
Well, it takes around 4 to 5 years.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.310
So pilot training's the same, regardless of the era.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.940
Even as technology evolves, humans don't change.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.490
Indeed, this plane certainly isn't from this era.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.530
Would you like a ride in it, Admiral Yamamoto?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.200
Ooh, that would be wonderful.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.160
It's not a problem, right? Lieutenant Satake?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:41.420
Not at all. Isoroku Yamamoto...

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.920
Isoroku Yamamoto?!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.320
Such impudence! Kusaka!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.030
How dare you just barge in on an unidentified aircraft!

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:08.900
When did you become entitled...

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.610
...to ignore orders from your superiors?

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.030
And I hope your accident at Midway...

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.950
...wasn't an attempt to avoid the battle.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.210
And if that's true, you'll face a court martial!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.670
Oh, come on, don't get so worked up, Air Force Chief.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.920
He has come back to us after all.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.760
By the way Lieutenant Kusaka...

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:32.550
...according to your report, the ship known as Mirai...

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.550
...displays no intention of joining our side...

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.850
...and cannot be captured by force.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.350
Senior Operations Officer
Kameto Kuroshima

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.440
Do the crew members oppose the Imperial Japanese Empire?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.240
Its destructive powers...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.200
...supposedly parallels that of a fleet of carriers.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.330
If we had it on our side, together with the Musashi...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:01.620
...then it would be as if we had three Yamatos in our fleet!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:04.580
Combined Fleet Chief of Staff
Matome Ugaki

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.580
That would be superb!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.130
At present that's not possible.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.130
They may be from the future,

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.260
but they're still Japanese, right?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.180
They're the children of parents who experienced defeat,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.640
and been brought up in an American influenced society.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.690
The defeat, you say?!

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.110
Are you saying that our country, Japan, lost the war?!

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.110
That's preposterous!

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.690
On the 15th of August, Showa 20th year,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.280
...after a loss of 20 million soldiers and civilians...

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.580
...Imperial Japan will unconditionally surrender...

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.330
...to the Allied Forces.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.960
Unconditional surrender?!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.730
Know thy enemy.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.440
Barefoot, or with rubber-lined boots...

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.940
...he prowls the forest silently, and sneaks up on you.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.820
With guile and strict stoicism...

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.860
...he walks farther than we do,

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.820
...eats less than we do...

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.830
...and endures more pain than we could.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.330
The Japanese soldier is...

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.750
...the world's greatest jungle soldier.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.920
Those men are not human.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.300
Do Japanese soldiers look like this?

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:34.380
Looks like something from Halloween.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.760
Or monsters out of a fantasy novel.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.470
I saw a Japanese in San Francisco once.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.260
He was small and looked like a monkey.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.270
I just don't get why...

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.310
...a country as small as theirs...

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.350
...would want to start a war with China.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.310
What's more, they're good at ambushes.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.980
If you're ambushed in the jungle, what then?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.860
Nothing to worry about.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.240
Do it just like in training.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.200
Attention!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.830
Aah, at ease.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.330
Sir!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.840
Tomorrow, the 1st Marines will have its first campaign!

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.500
- Oh, Vandegrift!
- That old man?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.210
The Major General!

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.590
Division Chief sir!

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.590
Are the Japanese really that formidable?

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.010
The pamphlet here says they aren't human.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.060
No matter how many you kill,

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.680
...they'll just keep coming, just like ants?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.560
The Japanese are human, just like you.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.440
Yes. But then-

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:34.020
They are soldiers of a totalitarian regime...

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.240
...who move according to their Emperor's commands.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.900
Don't underestimate them.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:38.950
Yes, Sir!

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.990
They love their country, just like we do...

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:43.450
and they love their families just as much as we love ours.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.790
That's why, we must pay them the utmost respect,

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.620
without letting our guard down...

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.790
...while we eliminate them.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.340
Alright! Let's go get 'em!

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:59.800
We are the strongest Marine Division in the world.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.300
We're not afraid of the Japanese Army!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:06.220
US Marine Corps! US Marine Corps!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.060
US Marine Corps! US Marine Corps!

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.980
This marine division, myself included...

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.780
...has never had direct contact with the Japanese.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:20.450
This is the First Division's maiden campaign.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.450
Our first battle.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.790
And I am afraid.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:32.580
But I will not tremble in front of my men.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.380
Don't you find it strange that...

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.550
...such a large ship has come so far unnoticed?

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.590
The soldiers are beginning to worry that...

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.800
...this is a trap to lure us to Guadalcanal.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:48.430
I have no idea.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.690
According to reports from the headquarters,

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:56.230
the Japanese Airstrip is heavily fortified and well protected.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:59.070
I'm expecting some fierce resistance from them.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:04.200
Nonetheless, Fletcher, head of the assault division...

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.160
...seems to be very afraid of the Imperial Navy.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.960
He has discontinued support and is planning...

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.250
...to withdraw his unit 72 hours after landing.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:20.260
We have to take the island within three days.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.130
This operation seems hopeless to many,

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.220
but no matter the cost, we need that island as a foothold.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:33.480
Claiming Guadalcanal will puncture the Japanese ego.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.070
The First Marine Division will be the first to cross the Rubicon,

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.610
and leave its mark in history.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:49.200
How dare he tell the Admiral what to do!

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.540
He's only a lieutenant!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.370
Japanese from 60 years in the future?

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:59.040
A cruiser called Mirai that can take down a carrier fleet?!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:02.090
60 years later America becomes a confederation?

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.930
And this Pacific War will...

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:09.050
The Empire will surrender unconditionally in three years?

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.180
Are you saying that you believed his preposterous stories!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.100
Chief Kuroshima?!

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.650
Haven't you seen that machine with your own two eyes?

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:21.230
Even Germany couldn't build an auto-gyro like that!

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.740
The biggest problem now is to keep that man a secret.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.250
Combined fleet Central Command.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:37.750
Not even the Navy Ministry can afford to ignore him now.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.000
Or refuse to listen to what he has to say.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:46.050
Even we have been made to sit at the same table as Kusaka.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.470
He didn't used to...

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:53.930
...show such disrespect to the Navy and his superiors.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.390
Chief Ugaki.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.980
Does knowing the future really bestow...

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.030
...that kind of power on a person?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.700
What will you do now?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.530
Will you return to the navy?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.950
If that's your wish, I can put in a recommendation for you.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:16.710
Sir.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.040
Or you can work under me.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.840
I will create a suitable post for you.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:27.170
Admiral, your freedom seems limited...

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.180
...in the middle of the combined fleet.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.720
Is that so?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.180
Compared to when I was the Deputy Commander on land...

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.180
...the ocean is a paradise.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.850
Spares me all the diplomatic functions.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.310
Thank you for your kind offer.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.980
But I am content with my present state.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.940
We listed you as KIA.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.490
If we send in a report, your family will be put at ease but...

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.490
...is there something you wish to do?

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.030
Yes.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.490
I need a favor from you.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:02.210
The war was started to secure Japan's survival.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.840
Without crude oil, its growing economy would collapse.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:10.180
We moved South for natural resources.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.300
But all of Asia's resources were already controlled by the west.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.270
Contesting the ABCD sphere of interest was inevitable.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.560
Right now, the Admiral is overseeing...

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:24.690
...the construction of an airstrip in Guadalcanal...

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.650
...south of the Solomon Islands.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.530
Using this as the base point against Allied forces...

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.570
...is the right decision.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:36.490
In this war, Japanese naval accomplishments...

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:41.580
...have served to remind Asians that Western superiority...

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.830
...is not absolute.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.000
In a way, I consider ourselves to have been victorious.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.630
But what I would really like...

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:55.050
...is for you to draw our defense forces...

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:59.730
...back to the Manchurian borders within the next year.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.360
Are you telling me to stop everything and run away?

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.730
No, I'll like to propose another strategy.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.860
Amazing!

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.570
It's fascinating!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.120
And it has the Red Sun on it!

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:22.870
Well, you mentioned that I have limited freedom.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.500
My freedom's limited by everything I am responsible for.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.760
You saw the future at the price of losing something to it.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:35.640
What did the encounter with the Mirai take from you?

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:40.140
The Japanese man, Takumi Kusaka, lost only his blindness.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:42.140
I see.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.060
Then what happened...

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.060
...to Navy Lieutenant Commander Takumi Kusaka?

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.110
Please take this.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:56.030
I have to return this to you.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.580
I wasn't the one who gave this to you,

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.540
but I'll keep it for you.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:14.050
Regarding the strategy that you proposed for Guadalcanal...

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.050
I will look into it.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.230
CIC response, set course 70 degrees.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.030
Surface Radar 15 miles, no object within radius.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.610
CIC response, set course 70 degrees.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.950
Roger.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.040
Turn to port!

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.830
Distance to Target Alpha, 50 miles.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.210
Target Alpha has reached Guadalcanal Western Point.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.210
Course and speed, 210 degrees and 10 knots.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.630
Formation unchanged.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:57.880
Approaching landing destination.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.140
Verification. Are they US Marines?

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:04.350
Guadalcanal, Allied Force Division for Tsuragi Operation.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.770
It's following history.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.150
No doubt about it!

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:10.360
0610...

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.030
...fleet commences attack.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.030
0614...

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.860
...3 hours of intense shelling ensued.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.530
Followed by the slaughter...

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.040
...of one man by another.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.370
Sea Eagle, according to schedule...

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:28.000
...will approach Guadalcanal from the South East.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.170
No targets in surrounding area.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.090
10 minutes to destination.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:37.510
I think they can make an undetected landing.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.890
I've come to realize the drawbacks...

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:41.890
...of our over-reliance on technology.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.560
If we had the GPS satellite system to guide the missile...

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.690
...there would be no need to land on the island.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.690
Is it better for us to send them in...

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.110
...after the shelling has stopped?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.490
No, it would be more dangerous...

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.990
...to have US aircraft circling the area.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.530
This is the best time to send them in.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.870
We're not well trained on land, however.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:09.580
Will a last minute team be able to complete the mission?

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.750
It's true that we're not trained on land, or in the jungle.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.050
Let's trust XO and Oguri's initiative.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.930
Altitude, 150 feet.

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:26.310
15 miles to the coastline.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.350
FLIR in action.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:29.810
Spot in sight.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.000
Drop off!

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.210
Gather in the front thicket!

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.510
Roll call!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.510
Lieutenant Oguri!

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:07.560
Here!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.100
Petty Chief Yanagi!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:09.730
Here!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.350
Officer Enomoto!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:12.060
Here!

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.860
Alright! Verify location!

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.780
Northeast of Guadalcanal, near Mt. Austen.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.950
Distance between here and the airstrip is 6 kilometres.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:30.290
At 0614, the Allied Forces will begin shelling this island.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.170
We will be waiting in trenches until the shelling stops.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.170
Finish your breakfast by then.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.710
Yes sir!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.960
I never thought I'd have to dig a trench in the navy.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:43.130
Commander, may I ask a question?

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.050
Go ahead.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:46.760
Just in case we get caught in the battle...

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.100
Which side should we be on?

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.930
We didn't come here for a fire fight.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:55.730
I want you to avoid any form of combat.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:58.440
And if we can't run away in time?

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.200
If that happens, the team comes first.

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:06.530
The top priority of this battle...

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.370
...is to respect your teammates' lives.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.080
Our lives should come before...

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.040
...20 thousand American and Japanese soldiers!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.210
Yosuke, I'm relieved.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:17.830
- You understand?
- Yes!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.250
Alright, then.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.210
Let's start digging!

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.060
That reminds me, the villagers didn't come today.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.020
They came every night before.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.650
I even memorized that dance of theirs.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.310
I have to admit that I do miss their company.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.110
I guess they could be busy with festivals or something.

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:44.110
Or busy in the fields.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.200
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:22.440
Just peacefully

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:34.220
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:47.130
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:53.730
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:59.810
I kept on praying

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:11.650
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:27.340
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.510
Trapped between life and death.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:43.560
You can only rely on your intuition and your luck.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:45.060
So this is the battlefield?

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:46.640
What is Kusaka planning?

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:48.350
Answer me! Lieutenant Tsuda!

00:23:48.350 --> 00:23:51.440
We have to drive out the US Marines from this island!

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:52.650
We're the only ones who can!

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:56.150
If our objective was to kill, we wouldn't be here at all.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:59.950
Operation Sagittarius aims at intimidation, not aggression.

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:03.160
Yosuke! In the end, Kusaka's still an Imperial Navy Soldier.

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:04.950
Next Episode: The Arrow of Sagittarius

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:04.870
Do not trust him!

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
